logs\codex-20261027T2310005256232Z-f25768cc7edc45669373b0aa380031f2.log:6484:Prepared procedure minimally succeeds the unchanged WU1 owner procedure. It reuses the existing issuer and runner, single-use claim slots, one-hour UTC authorization expiry, current-predecessor checks before prerequisite/issuance/runner, exact read-back, durable issuance/completion, transaction/session lock/timeouts, catalog/ownership/ACL and recovery/postcommit safeguards. It retains first-failure diagnostics, native exits, visible flushed logs and report/log read-back. Final clipboard delivery, exact ordinal read-back and OAF alerts remain delegated solely to the unchanged existing Invoke-OAFCodex host; offline preparation does not invoke that delivery helper.
logs\codex-20261027T2310005256232Z-f25768cc7edc45669373b0aa380031f2.log:6562:docs\WORKFLOW.md:251:The minimal issuer reads a UTF-8 JSON specification with exactly four keys: `request`, `artifact_approval`, `prerequisite_approval`, and `expires_utc`. `request` has exactly `action` (`verify` or `upgrade`), `environment`, `expected_start`, `target`, `manifest_hash`, and `revision_hash`. Both approval references have exactly `id` (canonical UUID) and `sha256` (SHA-256 of the approval file's exact bytes). `expires_utc` must be UTC, later than issuance, and no more than 24 hours later. Manifest/framework/revision hashes retain the existing `sha256-utf8-lf` normalization; approval-file and predecessor-claim hashes use exact bytes.
logs\codex-20261027T2310005256232Z-f25768cc7edc45669373b0aa380031f2.log:6563:docs\WORKFLOW.md:255:- `artifact-approval-<uuid>.json`: exactly `format` (integer 1), `kind` (`artifact_approval`), `id`, `reviewer_id` (canonical UUID), `approved_utc` (UTC), `decision` (`approved`), `manifest_hash`, and `revision_hash`. Approval must precede authorization issuance and match the independently reviewed artifacts. The repository manifest remains `pending_independent_review`; a future independent approval is a separate evidence record, never a change inferred from digest matching.
