logs\codex-20261028T0044337148261Z-e67ee9f4ea9c4e89a0db4aaf7b10f2d7.log:6728:docs/WORKFLOW.md:240:- **Policy C - authorization:** Require a distinct, deliberate owner-issued record with a unique UUID, UTC issuance and expiry, and lifetime of at most 24 hours. Bind the exact environment, operation, expected starting state, target revision, independently approved manifest/revision hashes, applicable prerequisite approvals, and predecessor claim. Reject missing, malformed, future-dated, expired, reused, mismatched, or stale records. Revalidate the exact bound authorization UUID, bytes, and UTC validity at the final runner and Alembic pre-mutation boundaries and immediately before commit, after required audit persistence. Matching hashes prove integrity only. The runner consumes records and never issues or approves them. Issuance is separate from artifact approval, and neither authorizes another environment or a later no-op.
